  "published": "2026-11-19T05:44:46.623Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "IRefreshTokenService.StartSessionAsync starts a session from any sign-in of your own: it creates the refresh token family and issues the first access token the way a refresh issues the next one (same lifetime, clock, expiry format and family_id claim), returning a SessionStartResult with the AuthResponse and the FamilyId. A custom IRefreshTokenService implementation must add it. EasyReasyClaimTypes names every claim type the library writes (RefreshFamilyId, TenantId, AuthType). The WebAuthn options and response types carry System.Text.Json converters, so they nest in an app's own request and response models: options write exactly their ToJson bytes whatever the host's options, a credential binds through the FromJson parser, and one that is present but malformed is a JsonException (400 from model binding). WebAuthn JSON is written with fixed settings of its own and no longer follows JsonSerializerSettings.CurrentOptions; the 64 KiB credential bound counts UTF-8 bytes. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/easy-reasy/blob/auth-v5.16.0/EasyReasy.Auth/README.md#migration-from-5150",
